Z||000000||kornholio||09-18-2000||11:18 PM||||Hi,<BR>Can a faulty fuel pump cause an engine to run rich?  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||09-18-2000||11:47 PM||||I doubt it - not by itself.  Plus, the fuel pump is the hardest thing to get to.  I'd first try testing for things like leaky fuel injector(s).||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-19-2000||12:01 AM||||Things that make EFI rich.....<P>Bad O2 sensor. cracked/leaking exhaust manifold. leaking injector(s). fuel pressure regulator. pinched fuel return line. bad vapor saver can.||||reg||1
